169	An easy-to-prove fact is that measurements remain measurements after post-processing their outcomes.
170	
171	\begin{proposition}
172	Let $A = \{A_a\}_{a \in \calA}$ be a set of matrices,
173	and let $f:\calA \rightarrow \calB$ be a function.
174	Then
175	\begin{equation*}
176	\sum_a A_a = \sum_b A_{[f(a)=b]}.
177	\end{equation*}
178	Thus, if~$\{A_a\}$ is a sub-measurement (respectively, measurement),
179	then~$\{A_{[f(a)=b]}\}$ is also a sub-measurement (respectively, measurement).
180	\end{proposition}
